-// Orthros (orthros-r17.patch, JSPI): the engine's waits for the game's files suspend it (WebAssembly JSPI, -sJSPI,
-// link-openmw.sh) while the page fetches the bytes, instead of the page's thread spinning on shared memory (Orthros'
-// src/vfs/data-client.js fetchSync, wantWait): the page answers input, draws its own indicator and presents what the
-// engine drew so far. Linked after the system library (--js-library): fd_read and fd_pread replace libwasi's.
-//
-// Where it may suspend: only under the engine's promising exports — omw_pump_frame (the frame) and main() (the boot) —,
-// which say so (orthros_jspi_enter / orthros_jspi_leave, engine.cpp, main.cpp), one suspension at a time. Everything
-// else that reaches the engine reads synchronously, as before: a suspending import called outside a promising export
-// would throw (SuspendError).
-//
-// A read first waits a few ms on the page's thread (ENV OPENMW_ORTHROS_JSPI_SPIN_MS, 10 by default; play/index.html
-// ?jspispin=N): the page's store answers most of the boot's reads that fast, and a suspension costs a round of the
-// page's event loop each — the spike that suspended at once took 2 s more to the menu over ~1,700 store hits. That
-// short wait holds during the boot (main) and the engine's loads — its loading screen on (orthros_jspi_loading,
-// mwgui/loadingscreen.cpp: a save's load, a COE, a door, an exterior cell's) —, where the page's thread is what the
-// player has. In play, outside them, a read never suspends: it waits on the page's thread as before r17 (ENV
-// OPENMW_ORTHROS_JSPI_PLAY_SPIN_MS unset or negative; ?jspiplay=N: it may, after N ms there): a frame that suspends
-// presents nothing more meanwhile, and in play each suspension cost the frame its short wait, then the round to the page
-// and back, the page's thread having nothing to show for it — with 100 ms first, 2-3 of 3 measured minutes still had a
-// frame gap of 400-900 ms that r14's synchronous reads did not (2026-10-30, docs/openmw.md). A read
-// whose file is one the page streams (its node's `orthrosStreamed`: Orthros' src/vfs/emscripten-files.js, asyncReads)
-// asks `soon(position, length, spinMs)`: null when its bytes are in the page by then — read at once —, else a promise
-// the engine suspends on, the read itself then Emscripten's (doReadv: the page's pieces). The announced wait
-// (orthros_read_wait, components/vfs/manager.cpp orthrosReadWait) asks the page's globalThis.orthrosReadWaitSoon the
-// same way (its answer, or a promise of it), else calls orthrosReadWait as before — in play too, after the short wait: it
-// is a load's (a cell change's read-ahead comes before its loading screen). ENV OPENMW_ORTHROS_JSPI=0 (?jspi=0):
-// never suspends — every read as before r17. A build without JSPI (ASYNCIFY != 2) never returns a promise.
-//
-// A worker thread's read (Lua's update on its own thread, orthros-r14.patch; PROXY_SYNC_ASYNC: proxied to the page's
-// thread) is answered at once, synchronously, as before: the page's thread may serve it inside a wait for that very
-// thread (Worker::finishUpdate's futex wait runs the proxied calls), where no promise could settle — the read waits on
-// the page's thread when its bytes are missing (counted: proxied). Never a suspension there, never a deadlock.
-//
-// While the frame or the boot is suspended, nothing else enters the engine's state from the page: the page's calls
-// (Module._omw_*, Module._orthros_*, Module.ccall / cwrap's — but omw_save_settings, which reads no game file and
-// which the page's leaving persists at once after) and the engine's WebSocket events (multiplayer, MWMP::WebSocket:
-// "callbacks never interleave with a frame"; one whose socket was deleted or handler replaced by then dropped) are put
-// off, in order, to just after its end (a microtask once it returned: before any other task), 0 returned meanwhile
-// (Module.orthrosEngineBusy, Module.orthrosAfterEngine(fn)). Input events still reach SDL's queue at once (the html5
-// callbacks answer synchronously): the next frame reads them. The debug COE and teleport (engine.cpp) run at the next
-// frame's start, inside it.
-//
-// A loading screen's frame (orthros_jspi_present, mwgui/loadingscreen.cpp LoadingScreen::draw) is presented: the engine
-// suspends until the browser's next rendering update has run (a task posted from requestAnimationFrame: the engine
-// resumes after the update, never inside it), at most every ENV OPENMW_ORTHROS_JSPI_PRESENT_MS (200 by default;
-// ?jspipresent=N, 0: never) — a load's reads the browser's copy answers within the short wait suspend nothing, and its
-// loading screen, drawn, was shown only at the frame's end: a COE's whole load one frozen picture, as r16's.
-//
-// In a load, a read — and the load's progress (orthros_jspi_breathe, mwgui/loadingscreen.cpp) — also gives the page's thread a turn when the engine has not let it have one for
-// ENV OPENMW_ORTHROS_JSPI_BREATH_MS (100 by default; ?jspibreath=N, 0: never) — a suspension until a posted message
-// comes back, input and the page's timers run meanwhile —: a load whose reads the browser's copy answers within the short
-// wait suspends nothing, and its long stretches held the page's thread whole (a COE 3.7 s, a save's load 2 s, measured
-// 2026-10-30) where the page answered input as late as r16.
-//
-// Module.orthrosBlocked { count, ms, max, files: ms by path, waits, waitMs, proxied, proxiedMs, proxiedMax, play, playMs,
